# gcp-agent-registry datum

## Overview

**Google Cloud Agent Registry** is a centralized, unified catalog that lets you
store, discover, and govern Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers, tools, and AI
agents within Google Cloud. It corresponds to the governance pillar and
inventory of your agents, servers, and endpoints in Gemini Enterprise Agent
Platform.

**Status**: Pre-GA (Preview). Subject to Pre-GA Offerings Terms.

**URL**: https://docs.cloud.google.com/agent-registry/overview

## Purpose in b00t

GCP Agent Registry is designated as a **C-priority delegation target** for
cloud-based code review in the b00t executive delegation system. It allows
agents to:

- Discover and reuse existing agent skills and MCP tools across an organization
- Query the registry to identify available agent capabilities for code review
- Enforce governance boundaries across agentic fleets
- Standardize on MCP or A2A protocols for agent-to-agent communication

Referenced in:
- `EXECUTIVE-DELEGATION-TARGETS.md` — Code review (cloud) row
- `EXECUTIVE-DELEGATION-PLAYBOOK.md` — Delegation decision tree, item 6

## Priority Classification

| Priority | Type | Use Case |
|----------|------|----------|
| C | Cloud code review | When language-specific reviewers (kieran-*-reviewer) are unavailable or cloud-native review needed |

## Data Model

Agent Registry separates read and write operations:

- **Service** (writable) — Create, update, delete agent/MCP server/endpoint entries
- **Agent** (read-only) — Get, list, and search for autonomous AI agents
- **McpServer** (read-only) — Get, list, and search for MCP protocol servers
- **Endpoint** (read-only) — Get, list, and search for REST API endpoint targets

### Service Types

| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| Agents | Autonomous actors with skills (high-level capabilities) |
| MCP servers | Providers of standardized data resources and tools |
| Endpoints | Target URLs (REST APIs) accessed by agents |

## Auth Requirements

### GCP Service Account (Recommended)

```bash
# Create service account
gcloud iam service-accounts create agent-registry-sa \
    --display-name="Agent Registry Service Account"

# Grant Agent Registry roles
gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding <PROJECT_ID> \
    --member="serviceAccount:agent-registry-sa@<PROJECT_ID>.iam.gserviceaccount.com" \
    --role="roles/agentregistry.serviceAgent"

# Download key
gcloud iam service-accounts keys create ~/.b00t/gcp-agent-registry-key.json \
    --iam-account=agent-registry-sa@<PROJECT_ID>.iam.gserviceaccount.com
```

### Workload Identity Federation (Alternative)

```bash
# For GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, or other workload providers
gcloud iam workload-identity-pools create agent-registry-pool \
    --location="global" \
    --display-name="Agent Registry Pool"

gcloud iam workload-identity-pools providers create-oidc <PROVIDER> \
    --location="global" \
    --workload-identity-pool="agent-registry-pool" \
    --issuer-uri="https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com" \
    --attribute-mapping="google.subject=assertion.sub"
```

## Integration with b00t Delegation System

### Via mcp_b00t_mcp_b00t_agent_delegate

When delegating code review to GCP Agent Registry, use the standard
delegation contract from `delegation-language.datum.toml`:

```json
{
  "description": "Code review via GCP Agent Registry",
  "worker": "gcp-agent-registry",
  "capabilities": "code-review,agent-discovery,mcp-scan",
  "priority": "C",
  "deadline": "30"
}
```

### SCORE/EXIT signal format

```text
SCORE: PASS:gcp-agent-registry:review-complete
SCORE: FAIL:gcp-agent-registry:<reason>
EXIT_SIGNAL: true
```

## How to Use as a Code Reviewer Target

### 1. Discover Available Review Agents

Query the registry for agents with code-review skills:

```bash
curl -X GET \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth print-access-token)" \
  "https://agentregistry.googleapis.com/v1/projects/<PROJECT>/locations/global/agents?filter=skills:code-review"
```

### 2. Submit Code for Review

Register a code review task as an endpoint or MCP server resource:

```bash
curl -X POST \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth print-access-token)" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "displayName": "PR #1234 Review",
    "description": "Review changes in PR #1234 for security and quality",
    "agentType": "MCP_SERVER",
    "skills": ["code-review", "security-scan"],
    "annotations": {
      "repo": "my-org/my-repo",
      "pr": "1234",
      "priority": "C"
    }
  }' \
  "https://agentregistry.googleapis.com/v1/projects/<PROJECT>/locations/global/services"
```

### 3. Query Review Results

```bash
curl -X GET \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth print-access-token)" \
  "https://agentregistry.googleapis.com/v1/projects/<PROJECT>/locations/global/mcpServers?filter=annotations.pr:1234"
```

## Env Vars Needed

| Variable | Required | Default | Description |
|----------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` | Yes* | - | Path to service account JSON key |
| `GCP_PROJECT_ID` | Yes | - | GCP project ID for Agent Registry |
| `GCP_AGENT_REGISTRY_LOCATION` | No | `global` | Location (global or region) |
| `GCP_AGENT_REGISTRY_API_ENDPOINT` | No | `agentregistry.googleapis.com` | API endpoint |

*Required unless using workload identity federation or gcloud ADC.

## CLI Interface

The primary interface is the **gcloud CLI** + Agent Registry REST API.
There is no dedicated `gcloud agent-registry` command group yet (Pre-GA).
Use the REST API with gcloud auth tokens:

```bash
# Get auth token
TOKEN=$(gcloud auth print-access-token)

# List agents in project
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  "https://agentregistry.googleapis.com/v1/projects/$GCP_PROJECT_ID/locations/$GCP_AGENT_REGISTRY_LOCATION/agents"

# List MCP servers
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  "https://agentregistry.googleapis.com/v1/projects/$GCP_PROJECT_ID/locations/$GCP_AGENT_REGISTRY_LOCATION/mcpServers"
```

## Client Libraries

### Python (google-cloud-agent-registry)

```python
from google.cloud import agentregistry

client = agentregistry.AgentRegistryClient()
parent = f"projects/{project_id}/locations/global"

# List agents
agents = client.list_agents(parent=parent)
for agent in agents:
    print(f"Agent: {agent.display_name}")
    print(f"  Skills: {agent.skills}")

# List MCP servers
servers = client.list_mcp_servers(parent=parent)
for server in servers:
    print(f"MCP Server: {server.display_name}")
    print(f"  Tools: {server.tools}")
```

### Installation

```bash
pip install google-cloud-agent-registry
# or with uv
uv pip install google-cloud-agent-registry
```

## gcloud Setup

```bash
# Ensure gcloud is installed and authenticated
gcloud auth application-default login

# Enable the Agent Registry API
gcloud services enable agentregistry.googleapis.com \
    --project=<PROJECT_ID>

# Verify API is enabled
gcloud services list --enabled \
    --filter="NAME:agentregistry" \
    --project=<PROJECT_ID>
```

